# The Forms layer re-implements the public API of System.Windows.Forms and System.Drawing with their exact names,
# types and shapes, so Windows Forms code compiles against it unchanged. The design rules below would rename or
# reshape that API (keyword-like names such as Select and Stop, nested collection types, custom event handler
# delegates, array properties such as TextBox.Lines, settable collections, virtual members read in constructors
# such as DefaultSize), so they are off in this library. Everything else, including the naming and style rules of
# the repository, applies as everywhere.

